  "result": "I re-planned all three returned laws, and the validator accepts all 10 nodes. One of them, NRS-484B-307-8d, now carries an operator gap, so that law stays blocked until you decide it.\n\n- **NRS-484B-283 (1)(a), (1)(b), (1)(d)(1)–(4), 8 nodes:** these came back only because of a stale pin on `LVMC_11_30_060_A`. A repair session revised that node this iteration and it is accepted under the same id. So I re-emitted the 8 records exactly as they passed before, which pins them to the current version. They still compose `NRS_484B_287_1c` and `NRS_484B_287_1e`, which are not accepted yet (both are in node repair). So these 8 nodes will wait for those two.\n- **NRS-484B-307 (8)(d):** the law's figure \"two complete cycles\" can't be written as a literal the gate can check. The only operator that counts signal changes takes a plain number that the gate's literal check never sees. Faking a literal or dropping the figure are both forbidden. So I filed an operator gap on that span, the same defect as G87 on NRS-484B-307-9b. The record is otherwise kept as last repaired.\n- **NRS-484B-307 (8)(a), node `o2`:** it came back because its roles for the paragraph (c) words (right or left turn on red) didn't match the accepted `o3`. It now uses `o3`'s roles and wording word for word. `o1` and `o3` are accepted and left out of the file. Paragraph (c) is still read as releasing the subject from the duty to remain stopped, but no longer only once it is inside the intersection. A lawful right turn on red crosses the near crosswalk first, and that entry would otherwise have counted as a violation; one scenario now tests exactly that.\n\nTwo things need your decision:\n- **G87:** it now blocks both NRS-484B-307-9b and 8d. Either fix to the counting operator closes both: let its bound be a typed count, or have the gate's literal check read its plain-number bound.\n- **A known gap in `o2`'s paragraph (d) exception:** it is borrowed from `NRS_484B_307_8d`, which only starts once the rider is inside the intersection. So a rider who waited two cycles may be flagged while crossing the near crosswalk on the way in. Closing it means widening both yield nodes, `o3` and 8d, to start at the crosswalk. `o3` is accepted, so I left it alone.\n\nFiles are in `iter-004/plan/batch-02/`:\n- `blueprint.jsonl`\n- `PLAN.md`\n- `aggregates.jsonl` (empty; no law-local aggregates)",
